    "q-162809": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162809",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${z}^{2}+{x}^{2}=4$ and $x+2y=-2$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩=\\lambda ⟨\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨1,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {z}^{2}+{x}^{2}=4 \\\\ x+2y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)={z}^{2}+{x}^{2}=4,\\,h(x,y,z)=x+2y=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=4 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
